WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.140
- What do you feel like separates

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.300
this "John Wick" from the previous three?

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:08.300
- I feel like for the first
time, we see Ian's character...

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.660
- [Kelly] Vulnerable?
Or not vulnerable but--

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.460
- Where it gets personal for him.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:15.293
- Yeah.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.290
- And his trajectory
throughout the rest of the film

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:22.030
is about loyalty and friendship

00:00:23.136 --> 00:00:24.311
and, for the first time, revenge.

00:00:24.311 --> 00:00:25.485
- And how sneaky he is.

00:00:25.485 --> 00:00:26.850
- Well I think yeah, but also I think,

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.710
you know, they have a deep love for John.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:29.543
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:29.543 --> 00:00:30.376
- I mean like if he was--

00:00:30.376 --> 00:00:32.730
I think if you asked anybody
their top list of assassins,

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:33.930
he would be number one.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:35.520
- Yeah.
- Well and the person,

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:36.780
like they're a fanboy,

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.400
but he's like, he is.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.990
But this also goes deeper than that

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.280
'cause you don't quite never know

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.130
what the relationship between me and--

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:45.440
- [Kelly] But there's such--
- Keanu is in the--

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:46.273
- a loyalty and a backstory.
- Absolutely.

00:00:46.273 --> 00:00:47.106
- Yeah.
- And him,

00:00:47.106 --> 00:00:48.630
we feel protective of him.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.310
And when at the beginning of this movie,

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.800
you know, my world is taken away from me.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:53.633
- I know. That's what I'm saying--

00:00:53.633 --> 00:00:54.830
- That's where it becomes--
- Your character, yeah.

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:56.917
- As you said in episode one,

00:00:56.917 --> 00:00:58.200
"This time it's personal."
- Personal.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.330
- And also in addition
to just how incredible--

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:03.810
I mean, when I watched the
film, I was struck by how--

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:06.300
I mean, every one of
these films looks great.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:10.530
But how incredibly beautiful the entire--

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.450
especially a film that moves so much

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:16.170
and has so much almost relentless action.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:17.910
It's just stunningly gorgeous to watch.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.110
But the other thing for
me is the theme of--

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:24.960
family's such a huge theme
in this particular film,

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.940
more than any others, and-

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.530
- For y'all and for your individual-

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.450
- Well yeah, I was gonna
say literal family,

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.970
but also you see with the three of us

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:36.060
how it's not just the family
that you're born into,

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:37.440
but the family that you've created,

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.750
and how much we really are family.

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.460
- Yeah.
- Also, the fact that Chad

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:44.340
has done all four is very, very important.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:45.630
Hugely important.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:46.770
- It's a common thread.
- And he and Chad

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.390
have worked together for, you know...

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:49.750
- Since The Matrix.
- Coming up probably 30 years,

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:51.600
over 25 years, yeah.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:54.180
So there's a deep
understanding of each other

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.520
and a deep empathy for the story.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.140
And Derek Kolstad wrote something

00:01:58.140 --> 00:01:59.550
which I think you've been very true to

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:03.090
and expanded upon in a very mature way

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:06.150
and in a very, you know, adventurous way.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.744
It's just a shame we can't--

00:02:07.744 --> 00:02:10.200
I can't kill anymore people.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.060
- Yeah. Well you're sneaky.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.650
Let's not get past that.
- [Lance] Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:14.670
- I was like,

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:17.053
oh with the twist!
- No, I say it though.

